": "THE PROJECTIVITY BRIDGE IS THE GAP BETWEEN KLEIMAN'S th:main AND THIS PROJECT'S CLAUSE (1), AND IT IS UNFORMALISED -- so \"clause (1) is a theorem in the literature\" (my own I-1360, flatly) needs the qualifier \"for PROJECTIVE curves\".", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:19:39.786198+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1465", "title": "FOUR ROWS AND FIVE FILES PRICE THE SEAM'S TWO ANTECEDENTS AS TWO CONDITIONS TO BE MET AT SOME LUCKY V. THEY ARE ONE CONDITION: at a one-chart atlas the pair says exactly that the chart map is an ISO of big-Zariski sheaves, by one mathlib instance nobody had used here.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:19:39.398201+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1473", "title": "THE ASSEMBLY IS BASE-FREE CATEGORY THEORY: both directions close with Scheme/Field/Algebra/picEt/cover/descent ALL DELETED. The file self-assessment (\"change of coordinates, not a strengthening\") is CORRECT but understated -- the coordinates are generic, not geometric. Plus one false provenance sentence.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:19:38.594131+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0491", "title": "[persistent] HUMAN DECISION, BINDING (2026-07-28): the Jacobian headline is stated over an ARBITRARY field with NO rational-point binder. Branch (2) of I-0372 \u2014 ETALE-SHEAFIFY \u2014 is chosen and closed.", "kind": "protection", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:14:23.392259+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0838", "title": "[persistent] [persistent] REPRESENTABILITY PUSH, 2026-07-29 \u2014 the claim/lane protocol that makes 10 free-objective lanes not collide.", "kind": "protection", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T03:14:23.334600+00:00"